{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787347615393,"sessionID":"ses_fda1daed3ffeZ76o2z0rrfeMgg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_74eae3425a3242e3adf6b895","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/cyr/kernel/core/rt.cc","newString":"void *rt_malloc(uint64_t n) {\n    if (!n)\n        n = 1;\n    uint64_t need = ((n + sizeof(hdr) + 15) & ~15ULL);\n    int c = cls_of(need);\n    /* Every block is rounded to its FULL class size so any pop from a\n     * bin always satisfies the request -- no capacity surprises. */\n    uint64_t clsz = (uint64_t)1 << c;\n    hdr *h;\n    if (bins[c]) {\n        h = bins[c];\n        bins[c] = h->next_free; /* size/magic stay intact */\n    } else {\n        h = (hdr *)mm_alloc(clsz, 16);\n        if (!h)\n            return 0;\n        h->size = clsz;\n    }\n    h->magic = RT_MAGIC;\n    return (void *)(h + 1);\n}","oldString":"void *rt_malloc(uint64_t n) {\n    if (!n)\n        n = 1;\n    uint64_t need = ((n + sizeof(hdr) + 15) & ~15ULL);\n    int c = cls_of(need);\n    hdr *h;\n    if (bins[c]) {\n        h = bins[c];\n        bins[c] = h->next_free; /* size/magic stay intact */\n        need = h->size;\n    } else {\n        h = (hdr *)mm_alloc(need, 16);\n        if (!h)\n            return 0;\n        h->size = need;\n    }\n    h->magic = RT_MAGIC;\n    return (void *)(h + 1);\n}"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /home/cyr/kernel/core/rt.cc\n===================================================================\n--- /home/cyr/kernel/core/rt.cc\n+++ /home/cyr/kernel/core/rt.cc\n@@ -35,18 +35,20 @@\n     if (!n)\n         n = 1;\n     uint64_t need = ((n + sizeof(hdr) + 15) & ~15ULL);\n     int c = cls_of(need);\n+    /* Every block is rounded to its FULL class size so any pop from a\n+     * bin always satisfies the request -- no capacity surprises. */\n+    uint64_t clsz = (uint64_t)1 << c;\n     hdr *h;\n     if (bins[c]) {\n         h = bins[c];\n         bins[c] = h->next_free; /* size/magic stay intact */\n-        need = h->size;\n     } else {\n-        h = (hdr *)mm_alloc(need, 16);\n+        h = (hdr *)mm_alloc(clsz, 16);\n         if (!h)\n             return 0;\n-        h->size = need;\n+        h->size = clsz;\n     }\n     h->magic = RT_MAGIC;\n     return (void *)(h + 1);\n }\n","filediff":{"file":"/home/cyr/kernel/core/rt.cc","patch":"Index: /home/cyr/kernel/core/rt.cc\n===================================================================\n--- /home/cyr/kernel/core/rt.cc\n+++ /home/cyr/kernel/core/rt.cc\n@@ -35,18 +35,20 @@\n     if (!n)\n         n = 1;\n     uint64_t need = ((n + sizeof(hdr) + 15) & ~15ULL);\n     int c = cls_of(need);\n+    /* Every block is rounded to its FULL class size so any pop from a\n+     * bin always satisfies the request -- no capacity surprises. */\n+    uint64_t clsz = (uint64_t)1 << c;\n     hdr *h;\n     if (bins[c]) {\n         h = bins[c];\n         bins[c] = h->next_free; /* size/magic stay intact */\n-        need = h->size;\n     } else {\n-        h = (hdr *)mm_alloc(need, 16);\n+        h = (hdr *)mm_alloc(clsz, 16);\n         if (!h)\n             return 0;\n-        h->size = need;\n+        h->size = clsz;\n     }\n     h->magic = RT_MAGIC;\n     return (void *)(h + 1);\n }\n","additions":5,"deletions":3},"truncated":false},"title":"core/rt.cc","time":{"start":1787347615388,"end":1787347615391}},"id":"prt_026383e92001pxJapyujrOeQGI","sessionID":"ses_fda1daed3ffeZ76o2z0rrfeMgg","messageID":"msg_02637a0f5001H64MkDiMTU93xj"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1787347615400,"sessionID":"ses_fda1daed3ffeZ76o2z0rrfeMgg","part":{"id":"prt_0263826020016O7K89lNpdaYqP","messageID":"msg_02637a0f5001H64MkDiMTU93xj","sessionID":"ses_fda1daed3ffeZ76o2z0rrfeMgg","type":"text","text":"First import prints sane pointers, then dies mid-strcmp — but I've spotted the deeper allocator flaw: **bin pops don't guarantee capacity** (a block created for a smaller request can be reused for a bigger one). Making every block exactly its class size:","time":{"start":1787347609090,"end":1787347615396}}}
