{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787381521795,"sessionID":"ses_fda1daed3ffeZ76o2z0rrfeMgg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_6c12cc7645334d379f2739f3","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git add -A && git commit -q -m \"Phase 4: message ports + kernel service endpoints + crash isolation\n\n- arch/x86_64/ctx.S + core/ctx.cc: coroutine stack switch (callee-saved\n  regs + RIP); ctx_make crafts initial frame (RIP slot highest -- the\n  off-by-one cost a debugging round)\n- core/sched.cc: real cooperative RR over concurrent sessions on\n  private native stacks; per-session WASI state (argv/exit) in the\n  session struct; sid 0 = kernel; names, uid, capmask (ABI §7 bits);\n  sched_kill with CAP_KILL check\n- core/ports.cc: ABI §1 datagram ports (create/bind/send/recv, 4 KiB\n  cap, non-blocking recv, per-session handle tables); kernel replies\n  enqueue directly via ports_kernel_enqueue\n- core/kernsvc.cc: kernel-owned registry (LIST/CAPS/KILL/SPAWN from a\n  boot-preloaded image table), devman ENUM, power REBOOT/OFF;\n  capability enforcement + [audit] lines to serial per §10\n- wasi glue: kern_port_* imports in new 'kernel' namespace; sched_yield\n  is now a true context switch\n- main.cc preloads /boot/modules/{console,login}.wasm before EBS;\n  kmain spawns console -> login -> ppa(admin caps) + ppb, then runs RR\n- services/: console.wasm (owns 'console', relays to stdout),\n  login.wasm (stub auth, heartbeats survive console death)\n- guests/test_pp.go: two-role payload (ping-pong x3, registry LIST,\n  KILL console, isolation window); tools/hostp4.cc host driver\n- gate: TEST PASS (p4) = rounds ok=3 + sessions=4 + kill rc=0 +\n  login alive after kill + KERNEL-OK\" && git log --oneline | head -2","workdir":"/home/cyr/kernel"},"output":"7e7c2dd Phase 4: message ports + kernel service endpoints + crash isolation\ne5f8d61 MEMORY.md: Phase 3 gate green\n","metadata":{"output":"7e7c2dd Phase 4: message ports + kernel service endpoints + cras