{"type":"text","timestamp":1787381659743,"sessionID":"ses_fda1daed3ffeZ76o2z0rrfeMgg","part":{"id":"prt_0283f985a001boL17ERn6BzNVz","messageID":"msg_0283e0a02001OH20CsnqsfvZdw","sessionID":"ses_fda1daed3ffeZ76o2z0rrfeMgg","type":"text","text":"Phase 4 committed. Starting **Phase 5** — fs.wasm (FAT16/RAM-disk), dual-route file access, multiuser stubs, abi_ver checking, and VM retirement. First the ABI v1.1 bump (login identity-grant op, per the freeze rules):","time":{"start":1787381651546,"end":1787381659739}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787381659754,"sessionID":"ses_fda1daed3ffeZ76o2z0rrfeMgg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_875f032299974640b2f24575","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/cyr/kernel/abi/ABI.md","newString":"# abi/ABI.md — guest-facing interface contracts (v1.1)\n\nBinding on both kernel substrate and all services/guests. Changes require a\nversion bump here + note in MEMORY.md. All integers little-endian (wasm\nnative). No NUL-terminated strings anywhere: lengths are explicit.\n\"Window\" = a region of a session's linear memory the kernel assigns at\ninstantiation; guests never compute absolute addresses, only window offsets.\n\n## v1.1 changelog\n\n- §7 registry gains op 5 = LOGIN {u32 sid, u32 uid, u32 capmask} -> status.\n  Callable ONLY by the session that owns the \"login\" well-known name\n  (kernel-checked). Grants a session its post-authentication identity +\n  capability set; this is the sole mechanism by which capabilities are\n  issued (at login, never otherwise). Motivated by Phase 5 multiuser stub.\n- Service modules MUST carry a custom section `abi_ver` whose payload\n  starts with byte 0x01; the kernel refuses modules without it.","oldString":"# abi/ABI.md — guest-facing interface contracts (v1, FROZEN)\n\nBinding on both kernel substrate and all services/guests. Changes require a\nversion bump here + note in MEMORY.md. All integers little-endian (wasm\nnative). No NUL-terminated strings anywhere: lengths are explicit.\n\"Window\" = a region of a session's linear memory the kernel assigns at\ninstantiation; guests never compute absolute addresses, only window offsets."},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /home/cyr/kernel/abi/ABI.md\n===================================================================\n--- /home/cyr/kernel/abi/ABI.md\n+++ /home/cyr/kernel/abi/ABI.md\n@@ -1,12 +1,22 @@\n-# abi/ABI.md — guest-facing interface contracts (v1, FROZEN)\n+# abi/ABI.md — guest-facing interface contracts (v1.1)\n \n Binding on both kernel substrate and all services/guests. Changes require a\n version bump here + note in MEMORY.md. All integers little-endian (wasm\n native). No NUL-terminated strings anywhere: lengths are explicit.\n \"Window\" = a region of a session's linear memory the kernel assigns at\n instantiation; guests never compute absolute addresses, only window offsets.\n \n+## v1.1 changelog\n+\n+- §7 registry gains op 5 = LOGIN {u32 sid, u32 uid, u32 capmask} -> status.\n+  Callable ONLY by the session that owns the \"login\" well-known name\n+  (kernel-checked). Grants a session its post-authentication identity +\n+  capability set; this is the sole mechanism by which capabilities are\n+  issued (at login, never otherwise). Motivated by Phase 5 multiuser stub.\n+- Service modules MUST carry a custom section `abi_ver` whose payload\n+  starts with byte 0x01; the kernel refuses modules without it.\n+\n ## 1. Message ports (binding from Phase 4)\n \n Extra imports appended to the mini-WASI profile (prefix `kern_`):\n \n","filediff":{"file":"/home/cyr/kernel/abi/ABI.md","patch":"Index: /home/cyr/kernel/abi/ABI.md\n===================================================================\n--- /home/cyr/kernel/abi/ABI.md\n+++ /home/cyr/kernel/abi/ABI.md\n@@ -1,12 +1,22 @@\n-# abi/ABI.md — guest-facing interface contracts (v1, FROZEN)\n+# abi/ABI.md — guest-facing interface contracts (v1.1)\n \n Binding on both kernel substrate and all services/guests. Changes require a\n version bump here + note in MEMORY.md. All integers little-endian (wasm\n native). No NUL-terminated strings anywhere: lengths are explicit.\n \"Window\" = a region of a session's linear memory the kernel assigns at\n instantiation; guests never compute absolute addresses, only window offsets.\n \n+## v1.1 changelog\n+\n+- §7 registry gains op 5 = LOGIN {u32 sid, u32 uid, u32 capmask} -> status.\n+  Callable ONLY by the session that owns the \"login\" well-known name\n+  (kernel-checked). Grants a session its post-authentication identity +\n+  capability set; this is the sole mechanism by which capabilities are\n+  issued (at login, never otherwise). Motivated by Phase 5 multiuser stub.\n+- Service modules MUST carry a custom section `abi_ver` whose payload\n+  starts with byte 0x01; the kernel refuses modules without it.\n+\n ## 1. Message ports (binding from Phase 4)\n \n Extra imports appended to the mini-WASI profile (prefix `kern_`):\n \n","additions":11,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"abi/ABI.md","time":{"start":1787381659745,"end":1787381659750}},"id":"prt_0283fb84f001j9C3gkAv1V6hsC","sessionID":"ses_fda1daed3ffeZ76o2z0rrfeMgg","messageID":"msg_0283e0a02001OH20CsnqsfvZdw"}}
