{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1787382143333,"sessionID":"ses_fda1daed3ffeZ76o2z0rrfeMgg","part":{"id":"prt_02847194d0011ZqHoce2L1RUzr","messageID":"msg_02846f990001Ja7geMtlC4zy2K","sessionID":"ses_fda1daed3ffeZ76o2z0rrfeMgg","snapshot":"c18498a2c52fea59323d536ae106499eb9485b2f","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787382149260,"sessionID":"ses_fda1daed3ffeZ76o2z0rrfeMgg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_bd7fb5665c524faaa5adcc9e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"/* FS transport for kernel-routed preview1 path ops (abi/ABI.md v1.1,\n * Phase 5 routing decision: BOTH routes exist).\n *\n * The fs.wasm session exports:\n *   _fsbuf()     -> i32 offset of its request buffer in its own memory\n *   _fsrespbuf() -> i32 offset of its reply buffer\n *   _fsreq(req_len i32, resp_cap i32) -> i32 reply length\n * The kernel writes a framed request into that buffer, calls _fsreq on\n * the fs session's runtime (synchronous, serialized by fs_lock), and\n * reads the framed reply back. Framing: {u16 op,u16 seq,u32 uid,\n * u16 path_len, path bytes, payload...}. */\n#ifndef FSTRANSPORT_H\n#define FSTRANSPORT_H\n#include <stdint.h>\n\n/* returns reply len (>0) or negative on transport failure */\nint fs_call(const uint8_t *req, uint32_t req_len, uint8_t *resp,\n            uint32_t resp_cap);\n\n#endif\n","filePath":"/home/cyr/kernel/core/fstransport.h"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/home/cyr/kernel/core/fstransport.h","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"core/fstransport.h","time":{"start":1787382149226,"end":1787382149251}},"id":"prt_02847305c0014mJZhIoKBr6kBO","sessionID":"ses_fda1daed3ffeZ76o2z0rrfeMgg","messageID":"msg_02846f990001Ja7geMtlC4zy2K"}}
