{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787405297912,"sessionID":"ses_fda1daed3ffeZ76o2z0rrfeMgg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_a0fca2dac22a465ea697e07b","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git add -A && git commit -q -m \"Phase 5: fs.wasm FAT16 + dual routing + multiuser stubs; VM retired\n\n- services/fs: FAT16 (16 MiB RAM disk, kernel backend) split into\n  testable core (fscore.go, host 'go test' with injected block IO —\n  full flow PASS in 20ms) + wasip1 shell (main_wasm.go). Serves BOTH\n  routes: kernel-routed preview1 via _fsbuf/_fsreq sync exports, and\n  direct-port clients; paths rooted at /home/<uid> (admin sees /);\n  auto-vivifies /home/<u>; open/write/read/close/mkdir/stat/del/ls\n- ABI v1.1: LOGIN op (registry, login-owner only, grants uid+capmask\n  by session name), reply-channel convention (rname field), and\n  kern_blk_read/write as the managed-runtime block transport (§3\n  window retained for raw guests) — backend swap story intact\n- glue: path_open/fd_read/fd_write(>=3)/fd_close/path_create_directory\n  routed to fs over ports+fsroute (yield-based wait, no wasm3 re-entry);\n  per-session fd tables in sched_wasi_state; canonical request frame\n  {op,seq,uid,rname[16],pathlen,path,payload} unified across\n  kernsvc/glue/fs/login/clients after offset-collision bugs\n- devblk: eager 16 MiB RAM disk + devblk_rw; window polling retired\n- engine refuses modules without abi_ver=1 custom section\n  (scripts/add_abiver.py stamps every service+payload at build)\n- console/login/fs get bounded idle lifetimes so sessions drain and\n  KERNEL-OK prints; login v2 = static user table auth (admin/u1/u2)\n- RETIRED 8-opcode artifacts: core/vm, tools/vasm, programs/*;\n  kmain refuses non-wasm payloads; make test = smoke (g1),\n  gates now test-g1..g3, p4, p5a/p5b\n- gate: TEST PASS p5a (preview1 create/write/read /home/1/hello.txt)\n  + p5b (direct-port write/read/delete + u2->u1 denial) + all prior\n  gates green (g1/g2/g3/p4)\" && git log --oneline | head -2","timeout":60000,"workdir":"/home/cyr/kernel"},"output":"da43b41 Phase 5: fs.wasm FAT16 + dual routing + multiuser stubs; VM retired\nb9263a2 ABI v1.1 RATIFIED: canonical datagram header (op,seq,uid,rname), pinned block-window offsets, SETCONF op + CAP_CONF bit, LOGIN op, abi_ver section, managed-runtime blk imports; §11 v2 roadmap (reply caps, LIST/CAPS gating)\n","metadata":{"output":"da43b41 Phase 5: fs.wasm FAT16 + dual routing + multiuser stubs; VM retired\nb9263a2 ABI v1.1 RATIFIED: canonical datagram header (op,seq,uid,rname), pinned block-window offsets, SETCONF op + CAP_CONF bit, LOGIN op, abi_ver section, managed-runtime blk imports; §11 v2 roadmap (reply caps, LIST/CAPS gating)\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"git add -A && git commit -q -m \"Phase 5: fs.wasm FAT16 + dual routing + multiuser stubs; VM retired\n\n- services/fs: FAT16 (16 MiB RAM disk, kernel backend) split into\n  testable core (fscore.go, host 'go test' with injected block IO —\n  full flow PASS in 20ms) + wasip1 shell (main_wasm.go). Serves BOTH\n  routes: kernel-routed preview1 via _fsbuf/_fsreq sync exports, and\n  direct-port clients; paths rooted at /home/<uid> (admin sees /);\n  auto-vivifies /home/<u>; open/write/read/close/mkdir/stat/del/ls\n- ABI v1.1: LOGIN op (registry, login-owner only, grants uid+capmask\n  by session name), reply-channel convention (rname field), and\n  kern_blk_read/write as the managed-runtime block transport (§3\n  window retained for raw guests) — backend swap story intact\n- glue: path_open/fd_read/fd_write(>=3)/fd_close/path_create_directory\n  routed to fs over ports+fsroute (yield-based wait, no wasm3 re-entry);\n  per-session fd tables in sched_wasi_state; canonical request frame\n  {op,seq,uid,rname[16],pathlen,path,payload} unified across\n  kernsvc/glue/fs/login/clients after offset-collision bugs\n- devblk: eager 16 MiB RAM disk + devblk_rw; window polling retired\n- engine refuses modules without abi_ver=1 custom section\n  (scripts/add_abiver.py stamps every service+payload at build)\n- console/login/fs get bounded idle lifetimes so sessions drain and\n  KERNEL-OK prints; login v2 = static user table auth (admin/u1/u2)\n- RETIRED 8-opcode artifacts: core/vm, tools/vasm, programs/*;\n  kmain refuses non-wasm payloads; make test = smoke (g1),\n  gates now test-g1..g3, p4, p5a/p5b\n- gate: TEST PASS p5a (preview1 create/write/read /home/1/hello.txt)\n  + p5b (direct-port write/read/delete + u2->u1 denial) + all prior\n  gates green (g1/g2/g3/p4)\" && git log --oneline | head -2","time":{"start":1787405297903,"end":1787405297908}},"id":"prt_029a867f80019PJm5qrakNDnNI","sessionID":"ses_fda1daed3ffeZ76o2z0rrfeMgg","messageID":"msg_029a7f165001jlyRJTrEDEJQsu"}}
