{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787419535842,"sessionID":"ses_fda1daed3ffeZ76o2z0rrfeMgg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_69217289a105487090874760","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git add -A && git commit -q -m \"Phase 7: interactive userland — input/focus, init, shell, guests libc\n\n- core/input.cc: serial RX polled between quanta -> key records\n  {kind,mods,cp}; delivered ONLY to focused session; kern_focus_set\n  resolves target via port-creator, gated by CAP_FOCUS (bit3)\n- glue: kern_input_recv/kern_focus_set in 'kernel' namespace; input_poll\n  hooked into scheduler loop\n- boot: loader preloads init.wasm/shell.wasm + \\etc\\init.conf;\n  kmain spawns EXACTLY ONE session in init mode (conf rides as argv[1]);\n  legacy dual-payload gate mode retained for p4/p5 disks (console/login/\n  fs auto-spawned when present)\n- services/lib (kernel.services module): canonical kern wrappers —\n  ports, input, focus, argv, console-out ('guest libc', tracks ABI)\n- services/init: parses init.conf, SPAWNs console/fs/login/shell via\n  registry, focuses login\n- services/login: input-driven typed auth (login:/password: prompts,\n  echo user only), static table admin/u1/u2, grants identity to SHELL\n  session via registry LOGIN then moves focus to shell; legacy port-\n  creds path kept for testers\n- services/shell: key-line editor, built-ins echo/cat/ls/stat/\n  kill-session; cat reads via kernel-routed preview1 and relays content\n  through the console server (direct fd_write fallback if console died)\n- fs: seeds /etc/motd on fresh format; /etc world-readable through the\n  namespace (writes still admin-only); poll_oneoff now yields real\n  quanta (0 events) so Go runtimes survive fatal paths & idle GC\n- services get bounded lifetimes (idle/total caps) so sessions drain\n  and KERNEL-OK prints; scripts/run_p7.sh drives scripted stdin over a\n  QEMU serial pipe with wait-for-prompt sync\n- gate: TEST PASS (p7) = typed u1/u1 auth + focus->shell +\n  'Welcome to the capability microkernel.' relayed via console;\n  regression sweep g1 g2 g3 p4 p5a p5b all PASS\" && git log --oneline | head -2","timeout":60000,"workdir":"/home/cyr/kernel"},"output":"95a22d7 Phase 7: interactive userland — input/focus, init, shell, guests libc\n6a22fec MEMORY.md: Phase 5 gate green — Phases 0-5 all green; frame/blk-transport conventions + debugging rules\n","metadata":{"output":"95a22d7 Phase 7: interactive userland — input/focus, init, shell, guests libc\n6a22fec MEMORY.md: Phase 5 gate green — Phases 0-5 all green; frame/blk-transport conventions + debugging rules\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"git add -A && git commit -q -m \"Phase 7: interactive userland — input/focus, init, shell, guests libc\n\n- core/input.cc: serial RX polled between quanta -> key records\n  {kind,mods,cp}; delivered ONLY to focused session; kern_focus_set\n  resolves target via port-creator, gated by CAP_FOCUS (bit3)\n- glue: kern_input_recv/kern_focus_set in 'kernel' namespace; input_poll\n  hooked into scheduler loop\n- boot: loader preloads init.wasm/shell.wasm + \\etc\\init.conf;\n  kmain spawns EXACTLY ONE session in init mode (conf rides as argv[1]);\n  legacy dual-payload gate mode retained for p4/p5 disks (console/login/\n  fs auto-spawned when present)\n- services/lib (kernel.services module): canonical kern wrappers —\n  ports, input, focus, argv, console-out ('guest libc', tracks ABI)\n- services/init: parses init.conf, SPAWNs console/fs/login/shell via\n  registry, focuses login\n- services/login: input-driven typed auth (login:/password: prompts,\n  echo user only), static table admin/u1/u2, grants identity to SHELL\n  session via registry LOGIN then moves focus to shell; legacy port-\n  creds path kept for testers\n- services/shell: key-line editor, built-ins echo/cat/ls/stat/\n  kill-session; cat reads via kernel-routed preview1 and relays content\n  through the console server (direct fd_write fallback if console died)\n- fs: seeds /etc/motd on fresh format; /etc world-readable through the\n  namespace (writes still admin-only); poll_oneoff now yields real\n  quanta (0 events) so Go runtimes survive fatal paths & idle GC\n- services get bounded lifetimes (idle/total caps) so sessions drain\n  and KERNEL-OK prints; scripts/run_p7.sh drives scripted stdin over a\n  QEMU serial pipe with wait-for-prompt sync\n- gate: TEST PASS (p7) = typed u1/u1 auth + focus->shell +\n  'Welcome to the capability microkernel.' relayed via console;\n  regression sweep g1 g2 g3 p4 p5a p5b all PASS\" && git log --oneline | head -2","time":{"start":1787419535833,"end":1787419535839}},"id":"prt_02a81a88400151VxoVplc0t7i3","sessionID":"ses_fda1daed3ffeZ76o2z0rrfeMgg","messageID":"msg_02a8052bd001q0268PzAY5LTQJ"}}
